{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicit process start and direct paraphrase of the initial return action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action content faithfully captures the first conditional path's subject."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the alternative return path and the XOR decision point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n_cnt"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact reproduction of the counting/comparison step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard correctly extracts the 'complete' status condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard correctly extracts the 'incomplete' status condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b2->n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Jointly captures the damaged-items decision branch, condition guard, and corresponding email action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match of the packing step content."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match of the storage step content."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully restates the notification step for missing items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact reproduction of the inventory removal step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit termination signal mapped to end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match of the repair/restock step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the discard path decision, state description, and resulting email action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18",
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Jointly covers the final packing/storage decision and its two resulting state actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit second termination signal mapped to end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The customer is then emailed with replacement charges, and the process is complete."
      ],
      "justification": "Closing completion statement mapped to final end node."
    }
  ],
